# Every text file checks out as LF regardless of the cloning machine's
# core.autocrlf. Without this, a fresh clone on a Windows machine with the
# (default) core.autocrlf=true checks samples/rent-agreement.txt out as CRLF,
# while the LF copy embedded in samples/rent-agreement.ts (generated from it
# at commit time) stays LF -- and rent-agreement.test.ts's identity check
# fails. Real, reproduced: `git init` in an existing directory never runs a
# checkout, so files written directly to disk (as this repo's were) never see
# autocrlf's conversion; only a subsequent clone does.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
